        "topic": "Gas Laws",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2002",
        "question_text": "<p>According to Boyle's Law, the pressure of a given mass of gas is inversely proportional to its volume at constant temperature. Which of the following equations represents this relationship?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Boyle's Law states that $P \\propto \\frac{1}{V}$ at constant temperature, which can be written as $P_1V_1 = P_2V_2$ or $PV = k$, where $k$ is a constant. The correct representation is $P \\propto \\frac{1}{V}$.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
