        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Chemistry",
        "topic": "Chemical Equilibrium",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2002",
        "question_text": "<p>For the reaction $N_2(g) + 3H_2(g) \\rightleftharpoons 2NH_3(g)$, what is the effect of increasing the pressure on the equilibrium position?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>According to Le Chatelier's Principle, increasing the pressure shifts the equilibrium to the side with fewer moles of gas to reduce the pressure. Here, the left side has 4 moles ($1N_2 + 3H_2$), and the right side has 2 moles ($2NH_3$). Thus, the equilibrium shifts to the <b>right</b>.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
            {
                "option_id": "63824",
                "tag": "a",
                "text": "Shifts to the left",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "62795",
                "tag": "b",
                "text": "Shifts to the right",
                "is_correct": true
            },
            {
                "option_id": "35941",
                "tag": "c",
                "text": "No effect",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "27386",
                "tag": "d",
                "text": "Increases the rate of the reverse reaction",
                "is_correct": false
            }
        ],
