        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2002",
        "question_text": "<p>The volume of a fixed mass of gas is 400 cm\u00b3 at 27\u00b0C. What will be its volume at 127\u00b0C if the pressure remains constant?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Using Charles's Law: $V_1/T_1 = V_2/T_2$. Convert temperatures to Kelvin: $T_1 = 27 + 273 = 300 K$, $T_2 = 127 + 273 = 400 K$.<br>Substitute: $400/300 = V_2/400$.<br>Solving for $V_2$: $V_2 = (400 \\times 400) / 300 = 533.33$ cm\u00b3.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
            {
                "option_id": "29395",
